│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ fix_bulge_delta_boundaries                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ Bulge moves currently query the entire closed rectangle between the original edge and the │
│                          │ new parallel edge. This incorrectly counts fish on the original edge and/or new edge even │
│                          │ though those boundary fish do not always change inclusion status.                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ A bulge has the same score-delta strip semantics as moving an edge:                       │
│                          │ - expanding right/up includes the new boundary but excludes the old boundary;             │
│                          │ - shrinking left/down includes the old boundary but excludes the new boundary.            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The existing inclusive query can corrupt `m_count` and `s_count`, causing SA to           │
│                          │ accept/reject based on inaccurate objectives and potentially retain a polygon whose       │
│                          │ tracked score is not its actual score. Restricting the queried strip fixes the            │
│                          │ incremental accounting while preserving the geometry and runtime profile.                 │
│ num_applied              │ 2                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0165                                                                                   │
