│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ local_guide_sampling                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ The current static-guide snap chooses uniformly from every fish coordinate on the whole   │
│                          │ board. Most such moves relocate an edge or a bulge by tens of thousands of units, which   │
│                          │ tends to create self-intersections, excessively disruptive score changes, or proposals    │
│                          │ that cannot refine the current promising region.                                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Add a guide sampler that usually chooses a coordinate near the current edge coordinate in │
│                          │ sorted guide order. Its radius shrinks during annealing, allowing broad exploration early │
│                          │ while making fish-aligned local refinements late. A limited global-sampling probability   │
│                          │ is retained early so the search can still escape an initially poor rectangle or discover  │
│                          │ distant clusters.                                                                         │
│ num_applied              │ 3                                                                                         │
