│ patch_name               │ exact_boundary_deltas                                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ The incremental scoring currently counts both the old and new edge lines when an edge     │
│                          │ moves or a bulge is inserted. This is incorrect for fish exactly on a boundary: for an    │
│                          │ expansion, fish on the old edge were already inside and must not be added again; for a    │
│                          │ contraction, fish on the new edge remain inside and must not be removed.                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This matters especially because the search deliberately snaps edge coordinates to fish    │
│                          │ coordinates. Correcting the swept-strip query prevents score drift, improving SA          │
│                          │ acceptance decisions and ensuring that the retained best polygon corresponds much more    │
│                          │ closely to its actual judged score.                                                       │
