│ patch_description        │ The incremental score update for an added bulge currently queries the whole closed        │
│                          │ rectangle between the old and new edge. This counts fish on the old edge even though that │
│                          │ edge is unchanged when the bulge expands, and incorrectly handles which boundary is       │
│                          │ removed when the bulge cuts inward.                                                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This is especially harmful because the search deliberately snaps edges to fish            │
│                          │ coordinates. The annealer can therefore accumulate artificial score gains from repeatedly │
│                          │ counting fish that remain inside/on the boundary, causing it to retain polygons whose     │
│                          │ tracked score differs from their actual score.                                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Update the queried rectangle according to whether the bulge adds or removes area:         │
│                          │ - When adding area, exclude the old edge and include the new edge.                        │
│                          │ - When removing area, include the old edge and exclude the new edge.                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This keeps incremental counts consistent with the problem’s inclusive-boundary rule while │
│                          │ retaining the existing fast KD-tree delta evaluation.                                     │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0402                                                                                   │
