│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ local_guide_sampling                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ Static fish-coordinate guides are currently sampled uniformly from roughly 20,000         │
│                          │ coordinates. Most proposed edge moves therefore jump across a large portion of the board, │
│                          │ which is especially harmful after the polygon has developed many edges: such moves are    │
│                          │ frequently rejected due to intersections and do not provide effective local refinement.   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Sample static guides from a coordinate-distance window centered on the selected edge      │
│                          │ instead. The window is broad early in the search to retain exploration, then shrinks      │
│                          │ substantially for profitable local boundary adjustments. Fish coordinates and their       │
│                          │ adjacent coordinates remain the candidate set, so this preserves the important ability to │
│                          │ place boundaries immediately beside fish.                                                 │
│ num_applied              │ 3                                                                                         │
