│ patch_name               │ boundarysafe_sa                                                                           │
│ patch_description        │ This crossover keeps the stronger boundary-safe strip accounting from the inspiration     │
│                          │ program: when an edge or bulge moves, only points whose membership can actually change    │
│                          │ are queried. In particular, the old boundary is excluded for expansion and the new        │
│                          │ boundary is retained for contraction, preventing score drift for fish lying on polygon    │
│                          │ edges.                                                                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The implementation is compacted and uses:                                                 │
│                          │ - KD-tree rectangle counting for fast score deltas.                                       │
│                          │ - A coarse 2D Kadane initializer.                                                         │
│                          │ - Simulated annealing with edge shifts and orthogonal bulges.                             │
│                          │ - Local intersection checks plus final full validation.                                   │
│                          │ - Exact score recomputation before output for safety.                                     │
