│ patch_name               │ local_fish_guides                                                                         │
│ patch_description        │ Fish-coordinate snapping is currently uniform over up to roughly 30,000 coordinates. Most │
│                          │ such proposals move an edge across a very large region, causing frequent                  │
│                          │ self-intersections, poor annealing acceptance, and expensive broad KD-tree queries.       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Use sorted guide coordinates locally: primarily sample a coordinate within a rank window  │
│                          │ around the current edge coordinate, while retaining a modest probability of a global jump │
│                          │ early in annealing. This gives the search fine-grained fish-boundary adjustments,         │
│                          │ especially later in the run, without removing global exploration.                         │
