│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ raster_growth_polygon                                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ This replaces polygon-edge simulated annealing with a raster-region optimization          │
│                          │ approach.                                                                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The plane is partitioned into a 64×64 adaptive grid whose cut lines are shifted away from │
│                          │ fish coordinates. Each cell receives an exact weight: mackerels minus sardines inside it. │
│                          │ The algorithm performs many randomized connected-region growth trials, prioritizing       │
│                          │ profitable cells while allowing a small number of negative bridge cells when they connect │
│                          │ stronger areas.                                                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Every candidate remains a connected union of grid cells, has a controlled boundary        │
│                          │ length, and rejects diagonal-only contacts that could create invalid point-touching       │
│                          │ boundaries. The selected cell union is converted directly into a simple orthogonal        │
│                          │ polygon by tracing its outer boundary. This makes geometry validation far cheaper than    │
│                          │ repeatedly checking arbitrary self-intersecting SA proposals, allowing many more          │
│                          │ high-level region searches in the time limit.                                             │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
