│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ correct_incremental_boundaries                                                            │
│ patch_description        │ The score cache used by simulated annealing must exactly match the fish contained by the  │
│                          │ current polygon. The existing incremental updates include/exclude edge points             │
│                          │ incorrectly: fish on both old and new boundaries can be counted twice or removed although │
│                          │ they remain inside. This is especially harmful because guide coordinates intentionally    │
│                          │ target fish coordinates.                                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Introduce a swept-edge query which excludes the old boundary when adding area and         │
│                          │ excludes the new boundary when removing area. Apply it to translations and bulges, so SA  │
│                          │ acceptance uses correct mackerel/sardine deltas.                                          │
